 "notes": "Endpoints: the committed multi-file OpenAPI specs (public/openapi/read.yaml for /api/*, write.yaml for /api/v3 with servers /api/v3; path items are $ref to other files, which from-openapi now follows), scope = the files that register those APIs (src/routes/write/, api.js, admin.js). Nothing comes out right: the write API registers through a helper, setupApiRoute(router, 'post', '/x', mws, handler), and the read API through setupPageRoute(app, '/x', ...) which also creates the /api twin (custom-registrar, 365); admin.js builds paths from a parameter, router.get(`/api/${name}/config`) (prefix-as-param, 13); api.js does const router = express.Router(); app.use('/api', router) in the same function and the routes still come out without /api (mount-same-scope, 12). The precision sample (whole repo) adds: jQuery $.get(url, callback) in the browser code is taken for a route registration (call-taken-for-route). The ActivityPub, feeds and meta routes are on the root router and are right. Calls: the browser api module (public/src/modules/api.js) prepends /api/v3 unless the route already starts with /api, so api.put('/admin/tokens/x') comes out without it (prefix-in-client-wrapper); api.del() is not read as DELETE (verb-alias); $.ajax(url, {...}) is not seen (request-config-object). Expected calls = every call in two sampled admin files. Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): api.del is DELETE — and like the other api.* calls lacks the /api/v3 the module prepends (prefix-in-client-wrapper); $.get is a call, never a route. Since H2b's TS route wrappers (2026-10-17): setupApiRoute/setupPageRoute/setupAdminPageRoute (src/routes/helpers.js, (...args) destructured, router[verb](name, ..) and router.get(`/api${name}`, ..)) are read as route wrappers, so their calls are routes — the write API under /api/v3/* (each router returned by its module's exported function and mounted with router.use('/api/v3/users', require('./users')())), the read API's pages and their /api twins; Express's optional trailing parameters give the short form too. The scope grew to the files registering the read API (index.js, user.js, activitypub.js), and, under H2-D15, 62 real routes the specs leave out were added (the HTML pages of setupPageRoute, the ActivityPub routes, /compose, POST /email/unsubscribe/{token}, POST /api/user/{userslug}/uploadpicture, the optional short forms); the spec's POST /api/email/unsubscribe/{token} was removed (the code registers only the GET). What is left is prefix-as-param: the remountable prefixes (`/${name}/..` with mounts built at run time by a reduce over a list plugins can change) and /ping, /sping under ${relativePath} — wrapper calls with such a path make no route.",
